Requirements: 6   with obligations: 5   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] A review can be configured to run individual stages with a reasoning effort,
    the same way it can already give an individual stage its own model. The setting maps
    a stage's label to an effort value. A stage not in the map runs exactly as it does
    today, and with nothing configured every request the review sends is unchanged, so
    every response recorded before this change still replays. Configuring one stage
    changes only that stage's requests.
    -> stage-reasoning-effort-configurable  [functional/explicit]
       A review can be configured to run individual stages with a reasoning effort.
    -> stage-label-to-effort-map  [functional/explicit]
       The setting maps a stage's label to an effort value.
    -> preserve-unchanged-requests-with-empty-config  [compatibility/explicit]
       With no stage-effort configuration set, every request the review sends remains
       unchanged.
    -> replay-existing-recordings  [compatibility/explicit]
       Preserve replayability of every response recorded before this change.
    -> stage-config-affects-only-that-stage-requests  [invariant/explicit]
       Configuring one stage changes only that stage's requests.

[task-02] A run never quietly goes without the reasoning it was configured to use. If
    the provider would discard the requested effort for a stage's model, the run stops
    before calling it, with an error naming the stage and the model.
    -> reasoning-configured-use-is-preserved  [invariant/explicit]
       A run never quietly goes without the reasoning it was configured to use.
    -> stop-before-discarded-effort-call  [error_handling/explicit]
       If the provider would discard the requested effort for a stage's model, the run
       stops before calling that model.
    -> error-identifies-stage-and-model  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       If the provider would discard the requested effort for a stage's model, the
       resulting error names the stage and the model.

[task-03] The review's provenance records, for each stage, the reasoning effort in force
    and the temperature and seed that actually reached the provider rather than the ones
    that were asked for, since a provider may refuse a temperature on a reasoning call.
    Each call's usage records its reasoning tokens, so the cost the report shows
    includes them.
    -> reasoning-effort-per-stage  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       For each stage, record the reasoning effort in force.
    -> actual-provider-temperature-and-seed  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Record the temperature and seed values that actually reached the provider.
    -> usage-records-reasoning-tokens  [functional/explicit]
       Each call's usage records its reasoning tokens.
    -> reasoning-tokens-included-in-reported-cost  [functional/explicit]
       The report's displayed cost includes reasoning tokens recorded in each call's
       usage.

[exclusion-01] Which stages should use reasoning, and at what effort. No stage's default
    changes.
    -> no-stage-default-changes  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter any stage's default reasoning behavior.

[exclusion-02] A command-line option for the setting.
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       This is a scope exclusion naming work that must not be added: a command-line
